# Fixed defect 504, 2026-10-08 (lane b15-parse): a map value that opens
# with `{` alone on its line was read as a body in braces and refused
# three times. Below, shapes `heroes fmt` would lay out again, each told
# nothing now: the reproducer, its entries on one line; a map holding a
# map whose braces stand on lines of their own; an empty map over two
# lines. Then a map's own mistakes, told as a map's: a key with no `:`,
# told once where the base told three messages, and a trailing comma; a
# map alone as a statement is its own case, its one message the checker's
# (`fixedbugs-504-a-map-alone-as-a-statement-is-told-once`). And the
# boundaries, told as before: a `{` at a constant's own margin is Allman's
# habit, as under any head; one a level deeper than an `if` over a
# statement is Whitesmiths' body; and one over a typed binding at a
# statement's margin is a block in braces, no map.

constant AGES: {str: i64}
    {
        "ziggy": 42, "mars": 7
    }

constant NESTED: {str: {str: i64}}
    {
        "a":
            {
                "b": 1
            }
    }

constant EMPTY: {str: i64}
    {
    }

constant NO_COLON: {str: i64}
    {
        "a" 1  #~ expected_map_entry_colon
    }

constant TRAILING: {str: i64}
    {
        "a": 1,
        "b": 2,  #~ trailing_comma
    }

constant ALLMAN: {str: i64}
{  #~ missing_body
    "a": 1  #~ expected_end_of_line
}

function whitesmiths(x: i64)
    if x == 1
        {  #~ missing_body
        print(x)
        }

function a_block(x: i64)
    y = x
    {
        z: i64 @ 2  #~ expected_expression
        print(y + z)
    }

function main()
    print(AGES.len() + NESTED.len() + EMPTY.len())
